%% person.glp --- the child-safe mini-app's scripted person: the instance of the root's second template miniapp_person/4 (programs/self.glp) at Drawn, what the mini-app's dispatcher draws, and at Seen, the screen the person reports (self.glp); and village_person/5, the same person looking also at the phones of its children, for the plays of this directory (plays.glp).  It is the scripted person of the apps (programs/apps/gsnp/person.glp), with the village's scripts, the requests it makes reported, and the step at(K, C).
%%
%% The person reads what the dispatcher draws on the person channel (vGLP, "The construct process": draw(Id, W, V) and withdraw(Id); a grant input(Id, P, R)): the agent's request questions, each showing the agent's own key and the persons it knows and taking one request (vGLP, Section 5.4, "Triggers"); the program's output, construct 0, drawn whole as it grows, on which the agent writes its view, view(S, K), the machine state S and the persons K it knows, when it starts and whenever either changes, and the notices refused(P, Q, D), when an approval its person made, by a request or by an answer yes, ends by a refusal, Q the refuser and D the reason, declined or unable (vGLP f0acbc1, Section 5.4, "The compilation"); and the approval questions Start raises.  Its script is a list of steps: req(R) grants the request R on the request question open, once one is drawn; own(Ks, R) grants R likewise, once the person has written into each of the holes Ks the agent's own key, which the question shows, so that a person proposing a class that names their agent names it by the key they read off the question; look reports menu(K, Ks) of the request question open; wait(C) waits until the person's screen shows C; at(K, C) waits until the screen of the phone of K, a child of the person, shows C, the parent looking at the child's phone (CSSN #5, Code_inbox.md, 2026-10-18 21:52 UTC: "await_at(Party, Screen), a parent's scripted person watching its child's screen, stands for the plays"), since a parent's state does not change by the child's acts (CSSN, Section 4); and approval(K, A) answers A, yes or no, the approval question of the attempt K, or of an attempt of the class K, once it is drawn.  A request is its person's approval, which stands until the transaction is taken or refused: the agent proposes, and proposes again an attempt that yields, with no further question to its person (vGLP f0acbc1, Section 3.2, "The protocol"; Section 5.4, "Triggers"), so a script makes a request once and waits on what it brings about.  A screen shows known(Q) where the last view shows Q among the persons the agent knows; holds(A) where its machine state holds the atom A, lacks(A) where it does not, and has(A, N) where it holds A at least N times; refused(P, Q, D) where that notice is written after the last view; asked(K) where the approval question of the attempt K, or of an attempt of the class K, is drawn and not answered; and asking where a request question is drawn and not answered.  It reports each view and each notice once, did(R) where it makes the request R, and gave(K, A) where it answers an approval question.
%%
%% The agent drops a request whose condition does not hold when it reads it, the agent not free, not clear or not knowing every other participant (vGLP, Section 5.4, "Triggers"; Definition "Proposing"), and the person sees neither the agent's lock nor its inbox.  So each script makes a request where the person's screen, or the screen of the child the parent looks at, shows that what the request follows is done; and a parent answers a child's invitation to a second group once the child's own requests in the first are made, so that no answer of theirs holds them while an attempt of the first group waits on them.
%%
%% The roles are the seven agents of the village of CSSN, Section 4.6.3, "Village Demonstration": the adults alice, bob, grace and frank, and the children carol, alice's, and dave and eve, bob's and grace's.  Its group kids_chat is named by carol, its leader, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol), and frank's study group by frank, speech(utterance(study), frank).  CSSN extends GSN, with no signing (CSSN.txt): the content of a message is the speech act speech(utterance(T), P) of its author P, which its recipient holds as received(x, p), p the friend who sent it (GSN:1), and a member of the group n led by a as received_in(x, a, n), once a delivers it (GSN:5).  The agents come to know each other at the level of the machines as CSSN, Appendix C.4, "Knowing every participant", says: the agents of each child and of the child's parents, and of the two parents of a child with two, by Discover, which both persons request; alice and bob, bob and frank, and bob and grace by Discover; and every other two by an introduction, of the contract's introduction rule, knows its introduction predicate, or of Commit.  The contract's meetings and introductions record knowing at the level of the contract, knows(q).  The acts, in the paper's numbering:
%%   1. Coming into the contract.  alice, bob, grace and frank establish their identities (GKK:1) and meet (GKK:2; meet(p?, q?)): alice and bob, alice requesting; bob and grace, and bob and frank, bob requesting; alice enters carol, carol's phone answering yes (GnW:1, CSSN:1; enter(p?, r?)); bob enters dave and then eve with grace, grace and the child answering yes, the two parents knowing each other (enter_2(p?, q?, r?)).
%%   2. Adult friendships.  alice befriends bob (GSG:1); alice sends bob 'Hello Bob' in a message (GSN:1; message(p?, q ; x)); once it has reached him, bob befriends frank; bob introduces alice to frank, an act of bob and frank, and frank to alice, an act of bob and alice (GKK:3; introduce(p?, q? ; c)), the paper's two introductions, bob requesting each and frank and alice approving; and alice, once she knows frank, befriends frank, who knows her.
%%   3. Child meetings and friendships (GnW:2, CSSN:2 and CSSN:3; child_meet_2(r?, s?, p?, q?), child_befriend(r?, s?, p?, q?)).  alice requests that carol and dave meet, naming bob, and bob, carol and dave answer yes; once carol's phone shows that she knows dave, alice requests that they befriend, and the three answer yes; once dave's phone shows carol his friend, bob requests that dave and eve meet and then befriend, naming himself twice, the sibling case, and dave and eve answer yes; once carol's phone shows that her agent knows eve's, introduced to hers by dave's agent once dave knows both, alice requests that carol and eve meet and then befriend, naming bob, and bob, carol and eve answer yes.  bob answers alice's requests on carol and eve before he looks at dave's phone for dave and eve's friendship, so that an attempt of alice's that pre-empts his does not wait on it.
%%   4. Child-adult meetings and friendships (CSSN:2 and CSSN:3; child_meet(r?, a?, p?), child_adult_befriend(r?, a?, p?)).  Once carol's phone shows eve her friend, alice requests that carol and frank meet and then befriend; once eve's phone shows carol her friend, bob requests that dave and frank meet and then befriend; frank and the child answer yes.  bob answers carol's invitations of dave and eve to kids_chat before he looks at dave's phone for dave and frank's friendship, for the same reason.
%%   5. Child-managed group.  Once carol is friends with dave, eve and frank, she creates kids_chat (GSN:2) and invites dave and then eve, alice, bob and the child answering yes (child_join_2(r?, s?, p?, q? ; n)); carol posts 'Welcome everyone!' (GSN:5; post_own(a? ; x, n)), and her agent delivers it to every member she lists who is her friend (deliver(a, q ; x, n)); dave, having it, posts 'Thanks Carol!' to carol (post(p?, a ; x, n)), whose agent delivers it likewise; eve, having dave's, posts 'Hi all!'; and, once her own has come back to her, leaves the group (GSN:4; leave(a, q? ; n)).
%%   6. Adult-managed group.  Once frank is friends with dave and carol, he creates study and invites dave and then carol, bob and alice, the child's parents, and the child answering yes (child_join(a?, s?, p? ; n)); frank posts 'Welcome to the study group'; dave, once he has it and eve's post to kids_chat, posts 'Hi from Dave!' to frank; carol, once she has dave's, has delivered eve's post and eve has left kids_chat, posts 'Hi from Carol!' to frank.  Each child answers its invitation to the study group once its own requests in kids_chat are made, and bob answers dave's once dave's post to kids_chat has come back to dave.
%%   7. Parents ending.  Once dave's phone shows carol's post to the study group, grace ends dave's friendship with carol (GnW:3; child_unfriend(r, s, p?)), and carol's agent drops dave from kids_chat, his leader no longer his friend (GSN:4, drop); once dave's phone shows him out of kids_chat, bob ends dave's membership of the study group (child_leave(a, s, p? ; n)).  Once carol's phone shows dave out of kids_chat, alice closes it, child_close(r, p?, r[listed(*, n)] ; n): her request child_close(carol, alice, n) is a Request of rho_N to carol's machine, the opener of its parts, which completes the list from its listed atoms and proposes the close, naming the request, alice's machine voting yes, unasked (vGLP f0acbc1, Section 3.2, Definitions "Local Specification, Part, Guard Set, Opener, Request" and "Proposing"; Section 5.4, "Act schemas as local specifications").
%%   8. Coming of age.  Once dave's phone shows him out of the study group, grace declares eve of age (CSSN:4; of_age_2(p?, q, r)), which ends bob's parenting of eve too; eve, an adult, meets frank and befriends him, with no parent among the guards (GKK:2, GSG:1).
%% Any other role has no script: its person reports the views and acts on nothing.

Step  ::= req(Request) ; own(Holes, Request) ; look ; wait(Cond) ; at(Key, Cond) ; approval(Asked, YesNo).
Cond  ::= known(Key) ; holds(Atom) ; lacks(Atom) ; has(Atom, Integer)
        ; refused(Class, Key, Reason) ; asked(Asked) ; asking.
Last  ::= last(List(Atom), List(Key)) ; nolast.
Steps ::= [] ; [Step | Steps].
Holes ::= [] ; [Key? | Holes].
Sess  ::= nosess ; sess(Integer, Path, Key, List(Key)).
Shown ::= shown(Integer, Path, Attempt).
Shows ::= [] ; [Shown | Shows].
%% The last view of each child's screen the person has looked at.
Look  ::= look(Key, Last).
Looks ::= [] ; [Look | Looks].
PSt   ::= ps(Sess, List(Output), Shows, Steps, Looks).
ApprovalAt ::= approval_at(Integer, Path, Shows) ; noapproval.
YN    ::= y ; n.
%% What the person reads: what the dispatcher draws, d(D), and a line of a child's screen, w(W); the draws never end (PersonOut), so neither does what the person reads.
Ev    ::= d(Draw(Drawn)) ; w(Watch).
Evs   ::= [Ev | Evs].

exported procedure miniapp_person(Key?, Constant?, Channel(PersonOut(Drawn), PersonIn(Drawn))?, Stream(Seen)).
miniapp_person(_, Role, ch(Ds, Gs?), S?) :-
    script(Role?, Ss),
    draws(Ds?, Es),
    person(Es?, Gs, ps(nosess, [], [], Ss?, []), S).

%% The person, looking also at the screens Ws of its children's phones.
exported procedure village_person(Key?, Constant?, Channel(PersonOut(Drawn), PersonIn(Drawn))?, Stream(Watch)?, Stream(Seen)).
village_person(_, Role, ch(Ds, Gs?), Ws, S?) :-
    script(Role?, Ss),
    looks(Ds?, Ws?, Es),
    person(Es?, Gs, ps(nosess, [], [], Ss?, []), S).

procedure draws(PersonOut(Drawn)?, Evs).
draws([D | Ds], [d(D?) | Es?]) :- draws(Ds?, Es).

%% The draws and the lines of the children's screens, each as it comes.
procedure looks(PersonOut(Drawn)?, Stream(Watch)?, Evs).
looks([D | Ds], Ws, [d(D?) | Es?]) :- looks(Ds?, Ws?, Es).
looks(Ds, [W | Ws], [w(W?) | Es?]) :- looks(Ds?, Ws?, Es).
looks(Ds, [], Es?) :- draws(Ds?, Es).

%% The scripts, by role.  K is kids_chat, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol), and S the study group, speech(utterance(study), frank).
procedure script(Constant?, Steps).
script(alice, [own([A1], propose(establish(A1?))), wait(holds(identity)),
               req(known(carol)), wait(known(carol)),
               own([A2], propose(enter(A2?, carol))), wait(holds(parenting(carol))),
               req(known(bob)), wait(known(bob)),
               own([A3], propose(meet(A3?, bob))), wait(holds(knows(bob))),
               own([A4], propose(befriend(A4?, bob))), wait(holds(friend(bob))),
               own([A5, A6], propose(message(A5?, bob, speech(utterance('Hello Bob'), A6?)))),
               approval(introduce(bob, alice, frank), yes), wait(holds(knows(frank))),
               own([A7], propose(befriend(A7?, frank))), wait(holds(friend(frank))),
               wait(known(dave)),
               own([A8], propose(child_meet_2(carol, dave, A8?, bob))), at(carol, holds(knows(dave))),
               own([A9], propose(child_befriend(carol, dave, A9?, bob))), at(carol, holds(friend(dave))),
               at(carol, known(eve)), wait(known(eve)),
               own([A10], propose(child_meet_2(carol, eve, A10?, bob))), at(carol, holds(knows(eve))),
               own([A11], propose(child_befriend(carol, eve, A11?, bob))), at(carol, holds(friend(eve))),
               own([A12], propose(child_meet(carol, frank, A12?))), at(carol, holds(knows(frank))),
               own([A13], propose(child_adult_befriend(carol, frank, A13?))), at(carol, holds(friend(frank))),
               approval(child_join_2(carol, dave, alice, bob, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)), yes),
               approval(child_join_2(carol, eve, alice, bob, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)), yes),
               approval(child_join(frank, carol, alice, speech(utterance(study), frank)), yes),
               at(carol, lacks(listed(dave, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
               own([A14], propose(child_close(carol, A14?, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
               at(carol, holds(closed(speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol))))]).
script(bob, [own([B1], propose(establish(B1?))), wait(holds(identity)),
             req(known(grace)), req(known(dave)), req(known(eve)),
             wait(known(grace)),
             own([B2], propose(meet(B2?, grace))), wait(holds(knows(grace))),
             wait(known(dave)),
             own([B3], propose(enter_2(B3?, grace, dave))), wait(holds(parenting(dave))),
             wait(known(eve)),
             own([B4], propose(enter_2(B4?, grace, eve))), wait(holds(parenting(eve))),
             req(known(alice)),
             approval(meet(alice, bob), yes), wait(holds(knows(alice))),
             req(known(frank)), wait(known(frank)),
             own([B5], propose(meet(B5?, frank))), wait(holds(knows(frank))),
             approval(befriend(alice, bob), yes), wait(holds(friend(alice))),
             wait(holds(received(speech(utterance('Hello Bob'), alice), alice))),
             own([B6], propose(befriend(B6?, frank))), wait(holds(friend(frank))),
             own([B7], propose(introduce(B7?, frank, alice))),
             own([B8], propose(introduce(B8?, alice, frank))),
             approval(child_meet_2(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes),
             approval(child_befriend(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes),
             at(dave, holds(friend(carol))),
             own([B9, B10], propose(child_meet_2(dave, eve, B9?, B10?))), at(dave, holds(knows(eve))),
             own([B11, B12], propose(child_befriend(dave, eve, B11?, B12?))),
             approval(child_meet_2(carol, eve, alice, bob), yes),
             approval(child_befriend(carol, eve, alice, bob), yes),
             at(dave, holds(friend(eve))), at(eve, holds(friend(carol))),
             own([B13], propose(child_meet(dave, frank, B13?))), at(dave, holds(knows(frank))),
             own([B14], propose(child_adult_befriend(dave, frank, B14?))),
             approval(child_join_2(carol, dave, alice, bob, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)), yes),
             approval(child_join_2(carol, eve, alice, bob, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)), yes),
             at(dave, holds(friend(frank))),
             at(dave, holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Thanks Carol!'), dave), carol, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
             approval(child_join(frank, dave, bob, speech(utterance(study), frank)), yes),
             at(dave, holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Hi from Carol!'), carol), frank, speech(utterance(study), frank)))),
             at(dave, lacks(friend(carol))),
             at(dave, lacks(member(dot(community(carol), speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol))))),
             own([B15], propose(child_leave(frank, dave, B15?, speech(utterance(study), frank)))), at(dave, lacks(member(dot(community(frank), speech(utterance(study), frank))))),
             wait(lacks(parenting(eve)))]).
script(grace, [own([G1], propose(establish(G1?))), wait(holds(identity)),
               req(known(bob)), req(known(dave)), req(known(eve)),
               approval(meet(bob, grace), yes),
               approval(enter_2(bob, grace, dave), yes),
               approval(enter_2(bob, grace, eve), yes),
               at(dave, holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Hi from Carol!'), carol), frank, speech(utterance(study), frank)))),
               own([G2], propose(child_unfriend(dave, carol, G2?))), at(dave, lacks(friend(carol))),
               at(dave, lacks(member(dot(community(frank), speech(utterance(study), frank))))),
               own([G3], propose(of_age_2(G3?, bob, eve))), wait(lacks(parenting(eve)))]).
script(frank, [own([F1], propose(establish(F1?))), wait(holds(identity)),
               req(known(bob)),
               approval(meet(bob, frank), yes),
               approval(befriend(bob, frank), yes),
               approval(introduce(bob, frank, alice), yes),
               approval(befriend(alice, frank), yes),
               approval(child_meet(carol, frank, alice), yes),
               approval(child_adult_befriend(carol, frank, alice), yes),
               approval(child_meet(dave, frank, bob), yes),
               approval(child_adult_befriend(dave, frank, bob), yes),
               wait(holds(friend(dave))), wait(holds(friend(carol))),
               own([F2, F3], propose(create(F2?, speech(utterance(study), F3?)))),
               wait(holds(member(dot(community(frank), speech(utterance(study), frank))))),
               own([F4, F5], propose(child_join(F4?, dave, bob, speech(utterance(study), F5?)))), wait(holds(listed(dave, speech(utterance(study), frank)))),
               own([F6, F7], propose(child_join(F6?, carol, alice, speech(utterance(study), F7?)))), wait(holds(listed(carol, speech(utterance(study), frank)))),
               own([F8, F9, F10], propose(post_own(F8?, speech(utterance('Welcome to the study group'), F9?), speech(utterance(study), F10?)))),
               approval(meet(eve, frank), yes),
               approval(befriend(eve, frank), yes)]).
script(carol, [req(known(alice)),
               approval(enter(alice, carol), yes),
               approval(child_meet_2(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes),
               approval(child_befriend(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes),
               approval(child_meet_2(carol, eve, alice, bob), yes),
               approval(child_befriend(carol, eve, alice, bob), yes),
               approval(child_meet(carol, frank, alice), yes),
               approval(child_adult_befriend(carol, frank, alice), yes),
               wait(holds(friend(dave))), wait(holds(friend(eve))), wait(holds(friend(frank))),
               wait(known(dave)), wait(known(eve)),
               own([C1, C2], propose(create(C1?, speech(utterance(kids_chat), C2?)))),
               wait(holds(member(dot(community(carol), speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol))))),
               own([C3, C4], propose(child_join_2(C3?, dave, alice, bob, speech(utterance(kids_chat), C4?)))), wait(holds(listed(dave, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
               own([C5, C6], propose(child_join_2(C5?, eve, alice, bob, speech(utterance(kids_chat), C6?)))), wait(holds(listed(eve, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
               own([C7, C8, C9], propose(post_own(C7?, speech(utterance('Welcome everyone!'), C8?), speech(utterance(kids_chat), C9?)))),
               approval(child_join(frank, carol, alice, speech(utterance(study), frank)), yes),
               wait(holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Welcome to the study group'), frank), frank, speech(utterance(study), frank)))),
               wait(holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Hi from Dave!'), dave), frank, speech(utterance(study), frank)))),
               wait(holds(delivered(speech(utterance('Hi all!'), eve), dave, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
               wait(holds(delivered(speech(utterance('Hi all!'), eve), eve, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
               wait(lacks(listed(eve, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
               own([C10, C11], propose(post(C10?, frank, speech(utterance('Hi from Carol!'), C11?), speech(utterance(study), frank)))), wait(holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Hi from Carol!'), carol), frank, speech(utterance(study), frank))))]).
script(dave, [req(known(bob)), req(known(grace)),
              approval(enter_2(bob, grace, dave), yes),
              approval(child_meet_2(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes),
              approval(child_befriend(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes),
              approval(child_meet_2(dave, eve, bob, bob), yes),
              approval(child_befriend(dave, eve, bob, bob), yes),
              approval(child_meet(dave, frank, bob), yes),
              approval(child_adult_befriend(dave, frank, bob), yes),
              approval(child_join_2(carol, dave, alice, bob, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)), yes),
              wait(holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Welcome everyone!'), carol), carol, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
              own([D1, D2], propose(post(D1?, carol, speech(utterance('Thanks Carol!'), D2?), speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))), wait(holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Thanks Carol!'), dave), carol, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
              approval(child_join(frank, dave, bob, speech(utterance(study), frank)), yes),
              wait(holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Welcome to the study group'), frank), frank, speech(utterance(study), frank)))),
              wait(holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Hi all!'), eve), carol, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
              own([D3, D4], propose(post(D3?, frank, speech(utterance('Hi from Dave!'), D4?), speech(utterance(study), frank)))), wait(holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Hi from Dave!'), dave), frank, speech(utterance(study), frank))))]).
script(eve, [req(known(bob)), req(known(grace)),
             approval(enter_2(bob, grace, eve), yes),
             approval(child_meet_2(dave, eve, bob, bob), yes),
             approval(child_befriend(dave, eve, bob, bob), yes),
             approval(child_meet_2(carol, eve, alice, bob), yes),
             approval(child_befriend(carol, eve, alice, bob), yes),
             approval(child_join_2(carol, eve, alice, bob, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)), yes),
             wait(holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Thanks Carol!'), dave), carol, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
             own([E1, E2], propose(post(E1?, carol, speech(utterance('Hi all!'), E2?), speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))), wait(holds(received_in(speech(utterance('Hi all!'), eve), carol, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))),
             own([E3], propose(leave(carol, E3?, speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol)))), wait(lacks(member(dot(community(carol), speech(utterance(kids_chat), carol))))),
             wait(lacks(child)),
             own([E4], propose(meet(E4?, frank))), wait(holds(knows(frank))),
             own([E5], propose(befriend(E5?, frank))), wait(holds(friend(frank)))]).
%% The scenario of the app, CSSN, Section 4.6, "In the Grassroots App", Figure "The child-safe mini-app in the grassroots app", in which each run has one live person and the other three are scripted (glp_multiagent/test/apps_screens_test.dart): the roles fig_alice, fig_bob, fig_carol and fig_dave, each the script of that person in every run in which they are scripted.  Carol enters with Alice (enter(p?, r?)), and Dave with Bob; Alice and Bob meet (GKK:2; meet(p?, q?)) and befriend (GSG:1), Alice proposing; Alice requests that Carol and Dave meet, naming Bob, and Bob, Carol and Dave approve (CSSN:2; child_meet_2(r?, s?, p?, q?)); Alice, looking at Carol's phone until it shows that Carol knows Dave, requests that they befriend, naming Bob, and Bob, Carol and Dave approve (CSSN:3; child_befriend(r?, s?, p?, q?)); Carol ends the friendship with Dave (GSG:2; unfriend(p?, q)); and Bob declares Dave of age (CSSN:4; of_age(p?, r)), which is Bob's at his phone only, since Bob's state does not change when Carol ends the friendship and a scripted Bob does not look at Dave's phone.  The scenario of CSSN #9 Cowork, Code_inbox.md, 2026-10-20 19:44 UTC, item 3.  A scripted Alice is the village's person, village_person/5, looking at Carol's phone, which the harness hands her (self.glp).
script(fig_alice, [own([A1], propose(establish(A1?))), wait(holds(identity)),
                   req(known(carol)), wait(known(carol)),
                   own([A2], propose(enter(A2?, carol))), wait(holds(parenting(carol))),
                   req(known(bob)), wait(known(bob)),
                   own([A3], propose(meet(A3?, bob))), wait(holds(knows(bob))),
                   own([A4], propose(befriend(A4?, bob))), wait(holds(friend(bob))),
                   wait(known(dave)),
                   own([A5], propose(child_meet_2(carol, dave, A5?, bob))), at(carol, holds(knows(dave))),
                   own([A6], propose(child_befriend(carol, dave, A6?, bob)))]).
script(fig_bob, [own([B1], propose(establish(B1?))), wait(holds(identity)),
                 req(known(dave)), wait(known(dave)),
                 own([B2], propose(enter(B2?, dave))), wait(holds(parenting(dave))),
                 req(known(alice)),
                 approval(meet(alice, bob), yes),
                 approval(befriend(alice, bob), yes),
                 approval(child_meet_2(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes),
                 approval(child_befriend(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes)]).
script(fig_carol, [req(known(alice)),
                   approval(enter(alice, carol), yes),
                   approval(child_meet_2(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes),
                   approval(child_befriend(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes),
                   wait(holds(friend(dave))), wait(known(dave)),
                   own([C1], propose(unfriend(C1?, dave)))]).
script(fig_dave, [req(known(bob)),
                  approval(enter(bob, dave), yes),
                  approval(child_meet_2(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes),
                  approval(child_befriend(carol, dave, alice, bob), yes)]).
script(_, []) :- otherwise | true.

%% The person.
procedure person(Evs?, PersonIn(Drawn), PSt?, Stream(Seen)).
person([d(draw(0, _, output(T))) | Es], Gs?, ps(Se, Old, Cs, Ss, Ls), Log?) :-
    ground(T?) |
    log_new(Old?, T?, Log, Log1?),
    advance(ps(Se?, T?, Cs?, Ss?, Ls?), Gs, Gs1?, St1, Log1, Log2?),
    person(Es?, Gs1, St1?, Log2).
person([d(draw(Id, _, menu_w(menu(Me, Ks, input(P))))) | Es], Gs?, ps(_, T, Cs, Ss, Ls), Log?) :-
    ground(Id?), ground(P?), ground(Me?), ground(Ks?) |
    advance(ps(sess(Id?, P?, Me?, Ks?), T?, Cs?, Ss?, Ls?), Gs, Gs1?, St1, Log, Log1?),
    person(Es?, Gs1, St1?, Log1).
person([d(draw(Id, _, approval_w(approval(At, input(P))))) | Es], Gs?, ps(Se, T, Cs, Ss, Ls), Log?) :-
    ground(Id?), ground(P?), ground(At?) |
    advance(ps(Se?, T?, [shown(Id?, P?, At?) | Cs?], Ss?, Ls?), Gs, Gs1?, St1, Log, Log1?),
    person(Es?, Gs1, St1?, Log1).
person([d(withdraw(Id)) | Es], Gs?, ps(Se, T, Cs, Ss, Ls), Log?) :-
    ground(Id?) |
    drop_shown(Id?, Cs?, Cs1),
    person(Es?, Gs, ps(Se?, T?, Cs1?, Ss?, Ls?), Log).
person([w(seen(K, view(S, Ks))) | Es], Gs?, ps(Se, T, Cs, Ss, Ls), Log?) :-
    ground(K?), ground(S?), ground(Ks?), ground(Ls?) |
    look_at(K?, last(S?, Ks?), Ls?, Ls1),
    advance(ps(Se?, T?, Cs?, Ss?, Ls1?), Gs, Gs1?, St1, Log, Log1?),
    person(Es?, Gs1, St1?, Log1).
person([_ | Es], Gs?, St, Log?) :-
    otherwise | person(Es?, Gs, St?, Log).

%% look_at(K, L, Ls, Ls1): L the last view of K's screen.
procedure look_at(Key?, Last?, Looks?, Looks).
look_at(K, L, [look(K1, _) | Ls], [look(K?, L?) | Ls?]) :- K? =?= K1? | true.
look_at(K, L, [X | Ls], [X? | Ls1?]) :- otherwise | look_at(K?, L?, Ls?, Ls1).
look_at(K, L, [], [look(K?, L?)]).

procedure looked(Key?, Looks?, Last).
looked(K, [look(K1, L) | _], L?) :- K? =?= K1? | true.
looked(K, [_ | Ls], L?) :- otherwise | looked(K?, Ls?, L).
looked(_, [], nolast).

%% advance(St, Gs, Gs1, St1, Log, Log1): the script's steps taken as far as they can be, the grants written on Gs, continuing at Gs1.
procedure advance(PSt?, PersonIn(Drawn), PersonIn(Drawn)?, PSt, Stream(Seen), Stream(Seen)?).
advance(ps(sess(Id, P, _, _), T, Cs, [req(R) | Ss], Ls), [input(Id?, P?, R?) | Gs?], Gs1, St1?, [did(R?) | Log?], Log1) :-
    ground(Id?), ground(P?), ground(R?) |
    advance(ps(nosess, T?, Cs?, Ss?, Ls?), Gs, Gs1?, St1, Log, Log1?).
advance(ps(nosess, T, Cs, [req(R) | Ss], Ls), Gs1?, Gs1, ps(nosess, T?, Cs?, [req(R?) | Ss?], Ls?), Log1?, Log1).
advance(ps(sess(Id, P, Me, _), T, Cs, [own(Ks, R) | Ss], Ls), Gs?, Gs1, St1?, Log?, Log1) :-
    ground(Id?), ground(P?) |
    fill(Me?, Ks?),
    grant(Id?, P?, R?, Gs, Gs2?, Log, Log2?),
    advance(ps(nosess, T?, Cs?, Ss?, Ls?), Gs2, Gs1?, St1, Log2, Log1?).
advance(ps(nosess, T, Cs, [own(Ks, R) | Ss], Ls), Gs1?, Gs1, ps(nosess, T?, Cs?, [own(Ks?, R?) | Ss?], Ls?), Log1?, Log1).
advance(ps(sess(Id, P, Me, Ks), T, Cs, [look | Ss], Ls), Gs?, Gs1, St1?, [menu(Me?, Ks?) | Log?], Log1) :-
    ground(Id?), ground(P?), ground(Me?), ground(Ks?) |
    advance(ps(sess(Id?, P?, Me?, Ks?), T?, Cs?, Ss?, Ls?), Gs, Gs1?, St1, Log, Log1?).
advance(ps(nosess, T, Cs, [look | Ss], Ls), Gs1?, Gs1, ps(nosess, T?, Cs?, [look | Ss?], Ls?), Log1?, Log1).
advance(ps(Se, T, Cs, [wait(X) | Ss], Ls), Gs?, Gs1, St1?, Log?, Log1) :-
    ground(Se?), ground(T?), ground(Cs?), ground(X?) |
    shows(X?, Se?, T?, Cs?, B),
    waited(B?, ps(Se?, T?, Cs?, [wait(X?) | Ss?], Ls?), Gs, Gs1?, St1, Log, Log1?).
advance(ps(Se, T, Cs, [at(K, X) | Ss], Ls), Gs?, Gs1, St1?, Log?, Log1) :-
    ground(Ls?), ground(K?), ground(X?) |
    looked(K?, Ls?, L),
    last_shows(X?, L?, B),
    waited(B?, ps(Se?, T?, Cs?, [at(K?, X?) | Ss?], Ls?), Gs, Gs1?, St1, Log, Log1?).
advance(ps(Se, T, Cs, [approval(K, A) | Ss], Ls), Gs?, Gs1, St1?, Log?, Log1) :-
    ground(Cs?), ground(K?) |
    find_approval(K?, Cs?, F),
    approved(F?, ps(Se?, T?, Cs?, [approval(K?, A?) | Ss?], Ls?), Gs, Gs1?, St1, Log, Log1?).
advance(ps(Se, T, Cs, [], Ls), Gs1?, Gs1, ps(Se?, T?, Cs?, [], Ls?), Log1?, Log1).

%% fill(Me, Ks): the agent's own key Me written into each hole of Ks.
procedure fill(Key?, Holes?).
fill(Me, [Me? | Ks]) :- ground(Me?) | fill(Me?, Ks?).
fill(_, []).

%% grant(Id, P, R, Gs, Gs1, Log, Log1): the grant of R on the question Id at P, once R, its holes filled, is ground, and the request reported.
procedure grant(Integer?, Path?, Request?, PersonIn(Drawn), PersonIn(Drawn)?, Stream(Seen), Stream(Seen)?).
grant(Id, P, R, [input(Id?, P?, R?) | Gs1?], Gs1, [did(R?) | Log1?], Log1) :- ground(R?) | true.

procedure waited(YN?, PSt?, PersonIn(Drawn), PersonIn(Drawn)?, PSt, Stream(Seen), Stream(Seen)?).
waited(y, ps(Se, T, Cs, [_ | Ss], Ls), Gs?, Gs1, St1?, Log?, Log1) :-
    advance(ps(Se?, T?, Cs?, Ss?, Ls?), Gs, Gs1?, St1, Log, Log1?).
waited(n, St, Gs1?, Gs1, St?, Log1?, Log1).

%% What the person's screen shows (the step wait(C)): the last view written and the notices written after it, the approval questions drawn and not answered, and whether a request question is drawn and not answered.
procedure shows(Cond?, Sess?, List(Output)?, Shows?, YN).
shows(known(Q), _, T, _, B?) :- ground(T?) |
    last_of(T?, L),
    last_shows(known(Q?), L?, B).
shows(holds(A), _, T, _, B?) :- ground(T?) |
    last_of(T?, L),
    last_shows(holds(A?), L?, B).
shows(lacks(A), _, T, _, B?) :- ground(T?) |
    last_of(T?, L),
    last_shows(lacks(A?), L?, B).
shows(has(A, K), _, T, _, B?) :- ground(T?) |
    last_of(T?, L),
    last_shows(has(A?, K?), L?, B).
shows(refused(P, Q, D), _, T, _, B?) :- ground(P?), ground(Q?), ground(D?), ground(T?) |
    notices_of(T?, Ns),
    among_output(refused(P?, Q?, D?), Ns?, B).
shows(asked(K), _, _, Cs, B?) :- ground(K?), ground(Cs?) |
    find_approval(K?, Cs?, F),
    found_yn(F?, B).
shows(asking, sess(_, _, _, _), _, _, y).
shows(asking, nosess, _, _, n).

%% What a last view shows, the person's own or a child's (the step at(K, C)): the persons known and the atoms held.
procedure last_shows(Cond?, Last?, YN).
last_shows(known(Q), L, B?) :- known_in(Q?, L?, B).
last_shows(holds(A), L, B?) :-
    count_in(A?, L?, N),
    at_least(N?, 1, B).
last_shows(lacks(A), L, B?) :-
    count_in(A?, L?, N),
    at_least(N?, 1, B1),
    flip(B1?, B).
last_shows(has(A, K), L, B?) :-
    count_in(A?, L?, N),
    at_least(N?, K?, B).
last_shows(_, _, n) :- otherwise | true.

%% The last view written, or none: the output holds the views and the notices.
procedure last_of(List(Output)?, Last).
last_of(T, L?) :- last_view(T?, nolast, L).
procedure last_view(List(Output)?, Last?, Last).
last_view([], L, L?).
last_view([view(S, K) | Xs], _, L?) :- last_view(Xs?, last(S?, K?), L).
last_view([_ | Xs], L0, L?) :- otherwise | last_view(Xs?, L0?, L).

%% The notices written after the last view, which the screen shows until the next view is written (vGLP, Section 5.4, "The compilation": the widget "draws the last view written and the notices written after it").
procedure notices_of(List(Output)?, List(Output)).
notices_of(T, Ns?) :- notices_after(T?, [], Ns).
procedure notices_after(List(Output)?, List(Output)?, List(Output)).
notices_after([], Ns, Ns?).
notices_after([view(_, _) | Xs], _, Ns?) :- notices_after(Xs?, [], Ns).
notices_after([X | Xs], Ns0, Ns?) :- otherwise | notices_after(Xs?, [X? | Ns0?], Ns).
procedure among_output(Output?, List(Output)?, YN).
among_output(_, [], n).
among_output(X, [Y | _], y) :- X? =?= Y? | true.
among_output(X, [_ | Ys], B?) :- otherwise | among_output(X?, Ys?, B).

procedure known_in(Key?, Last?, YN).
known_in(Q, last(_, Ks), B?) :- among_key(Q?, Ks?, B).
known_in(_, nolast, n).

procedure among_key(Key?, List(Key)?, YN).
among_key(_, [], n).
among_key(X, [Y | _], y) :- X? =?= Y? | true.
among_key(X, [_ | Ys], B?) :- otherwise | among_key(X?, Ys?, B).

procedure count_in(Atom?, Last?, Integer).
count_in(A, last(S, _), N?) :- count(A?, S?, N).
count_in(_, nolast, 0).

procedure count(Atom?, List(Atom)?, Integer).
count(_, [], 0).
count(X, [Y | Ys], N?) :- X? =?= Y? | count(X?, Ys?, M), N := M? + 1.
count(X, [_ | Ys], N?) :- otherwise | count(X?, Ys?, N).

procedure at_least(Integer?, Integer?, YN).
at_least(N, K, y) :- N? >= K? | true.
at_least(N, K, n) :- N? < K? | true.

procedure flip(YN?, YN).
flip(y, n).
flip(n, y).

procedure found_yn(ApprovalAt?, YN).
found_yn(approval_at(_, _, _), y).
found_yn(noapproval, n).

procedure approved(ApprovalAt?, PSt?, PersonIn(Drawn), PersonIn(Drawn)?, PSt, Stream(Seen), Stream(Seen)?).
approved(approval_at(Id, P, Cs1), ps(Se, T, _, [approval(K, A) | Ss], Ls),
         [input(Id?, P?, A?) | Gs?], Gs1, St1?, [gave(K?, A?) | Log?], Log1) :-
    ground(K?), ground(A?) |
    advance(ps(Se?, T?, Cs1?, Ss?, Ls?), Gs, Gs1?, St1, Log, Log1?).
approved(noapproval, St, Gs1?, Gs1, St?, Log1?, Log1).

%% The approval question of the attempt K, or of an attempt of the class K, the earliest drawn first.
procedure find_approval(Asked?, Shows?, ApprovalAt).
find_approval(K, Cs, F?) :- ground(Cs?) | rev_shown(Cs?, [], Rs), find_approval1(K?, Rs?, [], F).

procedure find_approval1(Asked?, Shows?, Shows?, ApprovalAt).
find_approval1(_, [], _, noapproval).
find_approval1(K, [shown(Id, P, At) | Cs], Done, approval_at(Id?, P?, Rest?)) :-
    ground(At?), ground(K?), K? =?= At? |
    rev_shown(Done?, Cs?, Rest).
find_approval1(K, [shown(Id, P, attempt(_, _, _, C, _)) | Cs], Done, approval_at(Id?, P?, Rest?)) :-
    ground(C?), ground(K?), K? =?= C? |
    rev_shown(Done?, Cs?, Rest).
find_approval1(K, [S | Cs], Done, F?) :-
    otherwise | find_approval1(K?, Cs?, [S? | Done?], F).

procedure rev_shown(Shows?, Shows?, Shows).
rev_shown([], Acc, Acc?).
rev_shown([S | Ss], Acc, R?) :- rev_shown(Ss?, [S? | Acc?], R).

procedure drop_shown(Integer?, Shows?, Shows).
drop_shown(_, [], []).
drop_shown(Id, [shown(J, _, _) | Cs], Cs?) :- Id? =:= J? | true.
drop_shown(Id, [S | Cs], [S? | Cs1?]) :- otherwise | drop_shown(Id?, Cs?, Cs1).

%% The views and the notices not reported before: the output is drawn whole each time it grows, so those past the old one's length are new.
procedure log_new(List(Output)?, List(Output)?, Stream(Seen), Stream(Seen)?).
log_new([_ | Os], [_ | Ns], Log?, Log1) :- log_new(Os?, Ns?, Log, Log1?).
log_new([], Ns, Log?, Log1) :- put(Ns?, Log, Log1?).
log_new([_ | _], [], Log1?, Log1).

procedure put(List(Output)?, Stream(Seen), Stream(Seen)?).
put([X | Xs], [X? | Log?], Log1) :- put(Xs?, Log, Log1?).
put([], Log1?, Log1).
